\code{multiScaleR_bayes} object, because a posterior has no single set of
estimates or maximized likelihood. Use \code{summary()} for posterior summaries
of the coefficients and scales, \code{\link[=posterior_scales]{posterior_scales()}} for the scale draws,
and \code{predict()} for fitted values with their posterior uncertainty.
\code{nobs()} returns the number of observations in the fitted data.
}

